# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# OpenShift 4.x — REHEARSED against recorded constraints, NOT live-installed.
#
# Evidence base (every non-obvious line below cites one of these):
#   R1  docs/engineering/openshift-parity.mdx — the subscriber's own
#       measurements of their restricted-v2 project + our parity matrix
#   R2  docs/engineering/openshift-parity.mdx § "Findings the genuine-OpenShift
#       run added (2026-08-21)" — MicroShift 4.18 rehearsal, genuine SCC admission
#   R3  docs/receipts/2026-08-21-m2-throwaway-test.md — the M2 kit run (LKE):
#       version pins, LimitRange/shm constraint values, Kyverno/cosign deltas
#   R4  station/profiles/TEMPLATE/ + docs/environments/openshift.mdx — the
#       shared-cluster tenant shape: registry pull-through proxy,
#       GitOps-by-commit, no CLI for the app team. (The filled profile that
#       grounded this lives with the account, not in this repo — ADR-0008.)
#
# PROFILE_TESTED is a two-value flag in install.sh ("yes" or anything else).
# The evidence supports "rehearsed against recorded constraints", which is not
# "yes": no OpenShift cluster has ever run kit/install.sh. See README.md here.
PROFILE_TESTED=no

# Documentation-only (install.sh does not read these; they keep the rung
# honest for anyone who sources this file or greps the provider set).
PROFILE_RUNG=rehearsed-against-recorded-constraints
PROFILE_EVIDENCE=docs/engineering/openshift-parity.mdx,kit/providers/openshift/README.md

# --- version pins -----------------------------------------------------------
# Same pins the M2 run exercised end-to-end (R3 §1). They are the pins the
# admission policy and the ApplicationSet were validated against; nothing
# OpenShift-specific argues for moving them.
ARGOCD_VERSION=v3.5.1
KYVERNO_VERSION=v1.19.0
# CAVEAT on ARGOCD_VERSION under restricted-v2: upstream Argo CD's own images
# hard-code UIDs (dex 1001, redis 999) and the SCC REJECTS them (R2). This pin
# installs clean only if you strip runAsUser from the upstream manifests. The
# supported path on OpenShift is the OpenShift GitOps operator — already Argo
# CD, already SCC-clean, already the house standard at banks (R1 "Deploys",
# R2). When the operator (or a house Argo) is present, run install.sh against
# it rather than letting step 2 install a second Argo.
# CAVEAT on KYVERNO_VERSION: the target cluster runs no Kyverno at all —
# cluster admission is the operations department's later hardening step, and
# the in-project verify gate is the enforcement point until then (R1, R4).
# The pin applies only where a cluster admin does install Kyverno.

# --- namespaces -------------------------------------------------------------
# install.sh defaults: ARGOCD_NAMESPACE=argocd, KYVERNO_NAMESPACE=kyverno.
# Deliberately NOT overridden here:
#   - The OpenShift GitOps operator owns `openshift-gitops`. Pointing
#     install.sh's Argo install at that namespace would have it apply upstream
#     manifests over an operator-managed instance — worse than the default.
#     Set ARGOCD_NAMESPACE yourself only when you are installing Argo (R2).
#   - A namespace-scoped Argo sharing the tenant project needs a namespaced
#     `*/*/*` Role beyond `admin` (escalation prevention blocks the tenant from
#     creating it) and its ~7 pods consume real project quota — size the
#     ResourceQuota for app + Argo, or give Argo its own namespace (R2).
# ARGOCD_NAMESPACE=openshift-gitops
# KYVERNO_NAMESPACE=kyverno

# --- registry ---------------------------------------------------------------
# REGISTRY_INSECURE stays unset: the target ingress is a Harbor pull-through
# proxy over TLS with a corporate CA, not plain HTTP (R1 "Registry", R4).
# Pass the CA with `--registry-ca <pem>` — Kyverno needs it as a trust bundle
# for signature fetch; --allowInsecureRegistry does not cover that TLS path
# (R3 "Deltas the live run forced into the kit").
# REGISTRY_INSECURE=

# --- constraints the preflight enforces on this provider --------------------
# Asserted offline against the recorded values in
# kit/preflight/tests/test_openshift_profile.py:
# - SCC restricted-v2 MUTATES (seccomp, drop ALL, assigns a UID from the
#   namespace range) and then REJECTS an explicit runAsUser/runAsGroup/fsGroup
#   outside that range. Measured on a real admitted bot pod in the target
#   project: runAsUser 1000920000, runAsNonRoot true, drop ALL, seccomp
#   RuntimeDefault, fsGroup set (R1). Deliver NO securityContext here.
# - PSA `restricted`, where a cluster also enforces it, additionally requires
#   runAsNonRoot — which the SCC never sets. SCC-clean is not PSA-clean (R3 §5).
# - The bot's memory-backed /dev/shm (2Gi) counts against its 2560Mi limit, so
#   the project LimitRange max must be ≥2560Mi; the recorded rig default
#   (64Mi default / 1Gi max) refuses the bot at admission (R3 §5).
# - OPEN PRODUCT FINDING, not fixed: under a random UID, `HOME` is absent from
#   the bot and agent-worker images at the v0.12.23 digests; the minio-init
#   sync hook fails (`mkdir /.mc: permission denied`) and the Application never
#   converges. `HOME=/tmp` is the one-variable fix, tracked upstream. No
#   preflight check detects this — P4 PASS does not mean the workload runs (R2).
